Services
Melbourne Eyecare Clinic is located in a purpose-built space, in the heart of the university precinct. Visit us for general eye examinations or for advanced eyecare and explore the broad range of services we offer to adults and children.

Teaching Clinic
Consultations at the Melbourne Eyecare Clinic are delivered by final year Doctor of Optometry students under the close supervision of our highly skilled and qualified optometrists. The teaching and learning component of our service provides the opportunity to reduce our fees for our services and products. Appointment times are longer than normal (up to 90 minutes) to allow for this learning and teaching component and close supervision.

Private Clinic
Our Private Clinic is co-located within the same facility as the Teaching Clinic. The Private Clinic is staffed by fully qualified optometrists with consultation appointment times running at the standard 30-45 minutes. You will be advised at the time of booking which private clinic times are available. The fees for our Private Clinic are in line with standard Melbourne metropolitan rates and will incur gap payments.

Appointments
When making an appointment you will be advised of the approximate time to allow for your visit.

Your appointment may require the use of dilating drops which may give you blurry vision for 4-12 hours post appointment. You may also be a bit sensitive to sunlight for this period, so bring sunglasses just in case!

