Our Difference
What makes us different? Melbourne Eyecare Clinic was established in 2009 by the University of Melbourne to provide excellence in clinical education for the next generation of optometrists and increase access to a comprehensive range of optometric services to the general public.

As a world class teaching clinic, our services are provided by postgraduate optometry students under the supervision of our highly qualified and experienced optometrists.

We provide a broad range of services to both adults and children.

For more information on the full range of our eyecare services please go to our Services page.

Book Now
Our Mission, Vision and our Values
We believe that as an organisation we want to be able to deliver and aspire!

To do that, we developed a mission to provide world-class education and training to our students and provide high quality, affordable and accessible eyecare services to the general public.

Our vision or our aspiration is to be recognised as an innovative, international leader in the provision of Teaching Health Clinics.

But we want to be able to provide our service while living and breathing the core values we set for ourselves. We will always strive to be ethical, accountable, collaborative and compassionate not just with each other but to all our customers and people with whom we do business.

